---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="Our privacy policy: cookieless analytics, no data resale, GDPR rights, and the sub-processors that operate this site.">
  <div class="container">
    <section class="hero">
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">Short version: we collect nothing that identifies you.</p>
    </section>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <section class="prose">
      <h2>Data we collect</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics 4 and cookieless analytics services described below.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Google Analytics 4:</strong> we use Google Analytics to
        understand how the site is used. It loads on page visit and may use
        first-party cookies and local storage to measure page views and group
        sessions. Google processes this data under its own privacy policy. See
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google's privacy policy</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>First-party telemetry:</strong> we also record aggregate page views,
        scroll-depth milestones, named button clicks, and outbound domains.
        The endpoint receives the page path, referrer when it is external, and
        a server-derived daily-rotating session hash. We do not use cookies,
        local storage, advertising identifiers, or user accounts.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics:</strong> a cookieless analytics
        service that reports aggregate statistics (page views, referrers,
        device types, approximate geographic region).
      </p>
      <p>
        These services answer the same question, "is anyone reading this?"
        not "who is reading this?" We use the data for aggregate reporting,
        not individual profiling.
      </p>

      <h2>Purchases</h2>
      <p>
        `<under development>`
      </p>

      <h2>Email</h2>
      <p>
        If you email us, we keep the correspondence to answer it. We do not
        add you to any list.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <p>
        The site is served by Cloudflare (hosting, HTTPS, and Web Analytics).
        Google processes analytics data through Google Analytics 4.
        Our first-party telemetry is processed by our Cloudflare Worker and
        D1 database. All other links are subject to their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under applicable law (including GDPR) you can request what data we
        hold about you; in practice, for this site, the answer is: none.
        Contact us via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>
        for any privacy question.
      </p>
      <p class="muted"><small>Last updated: 2026-08-31.</small></p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>